    <!--
      Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans). Machine translation, reviewed for consistency of
      terminology. Mainland conventions, matching how Android itself is translated:
      开发者选项, 无障碍服务, USB 调试, 无线调试, 通知, 快捷设置磁贴. "Revert" is 还原
      throughout, "revert to default" is 还原为默认, "hide/unhide" are 隐藏/取消隐藏.

      Two things in here are load-bearing rather than cosmetic:

      * The help page's menu paths have to name screens exactly as those screens are
        named in this file. A path pointing at a heading that does not exist in Simplified
        Chinese is worse than one left in English. The three entries under
        section_app_functions are settings_to_hide, revert_defaults_entry and
        accessibility_services.
      * The short strings used for bolding (help_name_*, notif_name_*, revert_defaults_entry,
        settings_to_hide_name_shizuku_hide, settings_to_hide_name_shizuku_watchdog) are
        matched as substrings inside the longer strings they highlight. Word them
        differently in the two places and the bolding silently does nothing.
    -->
